From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:14:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/54] hottyterm: a backdrop placement is drawn under the
 cells (V6-06)

hotty 0.6's V6-06: a placement with b=1 is a backdrop. hotty-blitz reads
the key, lists the feature `backdrop` once the terminal says it draws
them (hotty_host_set_backdrops), and passes each placement's backdrop to
the place callback. hottyterm draws one where kitty graphics draws an
image whose z is below INT32_MIN/2: after the window's background and
before the cells' (Ghostty's kitty_below_bg layer). A cell with the
default background is transparent over it, and any other background, the
text and the cursor cover it. Backdrops stack among themselves by z and
creation, under every other placement, and take no pointer: the hit test
leaves them out, so a press reaches the cells.

All of it is in src/termio/hotty.zig; no upstream file changes. It needs
hotty-blitz with V6-06 (its place callback carries the backdrop).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
